      "options": {
        "code": {
          "language": "plaintext",
          "showLineNumbers": false,
          "showMiniMap": false
        },
        "content": "# 0. Getting Started Guide\n\nWelcome! This harness helps you validate the Network Topology Exporter in your own lab.\n\n### 1. Get the Exporter\nDownload the latest release binary for your architecture from [GitHub Releases](https://github.com/colinedwardwood/network-topology-exporter/releases):\n- `topology-exporter-linux-amd64` (Standard servers)\n- `topology-exporter-linux-arm64` (Raspberry Pi / ARM)\n\n### 2. Configure the Stack\n- `cp deploy/test-harness/config.yaml.example deploy/test-harness/config.yaml` (Set your lab CIDR)\n- `cp deploy/test-harness/alloy/config.alloy.example deploy/test-harness/alloy/config.alloy` (Set your Grafana Cloud tokens)\n\n### 3. Launch with Docker Compose\n```bash\ncd deploy/test-harness\nexport SNMP_COMMUNITY=your_community\ndocker compose up -d\n```\n\n### 4. Verify\nOnce the box at the top turns **GREEN**, your data is being visualized in the other dashboards.\n\n---\n### Navigation\n- [01. Test Harness Health](./d/harness-health?var-tester_id=$tester_id)\n- [02. Topology Data](./d/topology-data?var-tester_id=$tester_id)",
        "mode": "markdown"
      },
      "pluginVersion": "13.1.0-25668120414",
      "targets": [],
      "title": "Onboarding",
      "type": "text"
    }
